  "cards": [
    { "dot": "cyan", "title": "One image, two processes", "items": ["web_a and web_b run the Next.js app behind nginx; the worker is the same image started as dist/worker.mjs.", "Web enqueues jobs in the same transaction as the change (pg-boss), so there is no outbox table.", "The worker revalidates caches by POSTing an HMAC-signed request to /api/internal/revalidate on every replica; nginx blocks that path from outside."] },
    { "dot": "emerald", "title": "Data stores", "items": ["PostgreSQL is the only system of record and also holds the job queue.", "Redis and Elasticsearch are optional copies: without them the app falls back to Postgres cache and full-text search.", "Database triggers notify the worker, which clears Redis stock keys and feeds the search index."] },
    { "dot": "amber", "title": "Outside the box", "items": ["Razorpay and Shiprocket call back into web through signed webhooks.", "Cloudflare Turnstile, Sentry and Google Analytics are also used but omitted from the drawing for clarity.", "Backups (pgBackRest and restic to Cloudflare R2) are on the deployment diagram."] }
  ]
